{
  "analysis": "The novnc site config looks correct — it serves static files from /usr/share/novnc on the root path and proxies /websockify to port 6080. However, the nginx.conf only includes mime.types and does not include sites-enabled or conf.d. That means our site config is never loaded. Nginx is using some other configuration (possibly a default in nginx.conf) that proxies to port 8080. I need to inspect the full nginx.conf and add the proper include directive.",
  "plan": "Show the full nginx.conf to find the server block that proxies to 8080. Then either add an include for sites-enabled or replace the server block in nginx.conf with our noVNC configuration. Reload nginx and re-test.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat -n /etc/nginx/nginx.conf\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
